.TH PERSONALITY_ELKS 7 "March 2026" "Substrate" "Miscellaneous Information Manual"
.SH NAME
personality_elks \- Substrate ELKS personality developer guide
.SH DESCRIPTION
The
.B ELKS
personality allows Substrate on i386 to execute 16-bit protected-mode ELKS
programs through a private per-process LDT and an ELKS-specific syscall and
signal ABI translation layer.
.PP
ELKS execution in Substrate is not VM86 emulation and is not Linux i386 ABI
compatibility. It is a distinct 16-bit personality with its own loader,
process-entry image, signal delivery path, and syscall table.
.SH EXECUTION MODEL
An ELKS process:
.IP \(bu 2
is recognized from a Minix-style 16-bit
.BR a.out
header
.IP \(bu
runs with
.B PERS_ELKS
and
.B BITNESS_16
.IP \(bu
enters userspace through ring-3 LDT-backed 16-bit segments
.IP \(bu
invokes syscalls through
.BR INT\ 0x80
.PP
The loader constructs a 16-bit startup stack image containing:
.IP \(bu 2
16-bit
.B argc
.IP \(bu
16-bit
.B argv[]
vector
.IP \(bu
16-bit
.B envp[]
vector
.IP \(bu
NUL-terminated argument and environment strings
.SH SIGNALS
Native Substrate signal semantics remain the kernel source of truth.
The ELKS personality translates ELKS smallsig numbers at the personality
boundary.
.PP
Signal delivery does not use the native i386 signal trampoline ABI.
Instead, the kernel builds an ELKS far-return frame for the ELKS libc callback
convention, so the userspace callback returns with
.BR lret\ $2 .
.SH CURRENT SUPPORTED RUNTIME
The current in-tree ELKS runtime supports, and has boot smoke coverage for:
.IP \(bu 2
console write and read/write syscalls
.IP \(bu
open, creat, close, unlink on ext2 root
.IP \(bu
fork and waitpid
.IP \(bu
alarm, pause, and ELKS-style signal callback delivery
.SH LIMITATIONS
Current limitations include:
.IP \(bu 2
incomplete syscall coverage outside the active translated table
.IP \(bu
ELKS crash handling currently captures 16-bit register and LDT-segment state
through the generic kernel core-dump hook; persistent core-file emission is not
yet implemented
.IP \(bu
incomplete fault-isolation validation for LDT bounds violations
.IP \(bu
no completed ELKS userland compatibility claim beyond the smoke-tested binaries
